# Food Munch Website 

## About the Project

Food Munch is a responsive food website created using HTML, CSS, Bootstrap, and JavaScript. It displays food menu options and provides information about food services, delivery, and payment methods.

This project was developed as a front-end web development project for learning and portfolio purposes.

## Technologies Used

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Bootstrap 4
- JavaScript
- Font Awesome
- Relevant images

## Project Structure

The project contains three main files:

- `index.html` — contains the structure and content of the website.
- `style.css` — controls the colours, layout, spacing, and overall design.
- `app.js` — handles interactive features and smooth scrolling.

## Features

- Responsive navigation bar
- Food menu with images
- Food service and healthy food sections
- Delivery and payment information
- Interactive gift pop-up
- Social media links
- Navigation to different website sections
- Responsive design for desktop and mobile screens

## How to Run the Project

1. Download or copy the project files to your computer.
2. Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
3. Make sure `index.html`, `style.css`, and `app.js` are in the same folder.
4. Open `index.html` using the Live Server extension.
5. The website will open in your browser.

An internet connection is needed to load the external images and online libraries.

## Project Limitations

This is a front-end demonstration website. It does not support real food ordering, online payments, or order tracking. The social media links are sample links.

